{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural","id":1151640,"title":"[2E] Vampire blood effects on other supernatural","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-21T08:06:45-07:00","id":1151640,"title":"[2E] Vampire blood effects on other supernatural","content":"I want to dwell deeper in my crossover game on Kindred's blood on other 'monster races', particularity Uratha. <b>Is there some 2E sum up of how Vitea affects monsters across gamelines? </b>In particular, what are effects on werewolves - do vampire's blood can heal instantly Aggravated damage? Because Uratha in 2E can easily heal Lethal damages in matter of hours on they own, so I do not see any benfit for werewolves to drink blood of Kindred...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-21-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:08:16-07:00","id":1151653,"title":"","content":"On the Aggravated, no. Vampire blood can cause addiction and blood bond in other supernaturals. It can't make ghouls out of them, tho. This has been repeatedly stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:55:13-07:00","id":1151665,"title":"","content":"So werewolves will not get anything from drinking vampires? \ud83d\ude10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T10:03:54-07:00","id":1151669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151665#post1151665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So werewolves will not get anything from drinking vampires? \ud83d\ude10</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T10:14:00-07:00","id":1151671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151665#post1151665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So werewolves will not get anything from drinking vampires? \ud83d\ude10</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically no, but, what do we &quot;mechanically&quot; get out of any drug? That's not why we take them, or want other people addicted to them on our behalf. Speaking for the narrative, the werewolves could think they get a <i>lot</i> out of drinking blood from a vampire, thinking it makes them stronger, faster, or whatever--but it could all be a placebo, built on the powerful lie their addiction is giving them, and the overwhelming feelings it forces them to have for their vampire dealer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T10:26:16-07:00","id":1151673,"title":"","content":"Probably nothing acutally useful would come out of it. It can't ghouls major templates, but I assume they could still get Vitae addicted. Werewolves might be more prone to Death Rage, and willingly drinking vampire blood can't be good for a Changeling's Clarity. Argentum-following Prometheans might actually <i>benefit</i> from experiencing Vitae addiction, in that it could assist in the Pilgrimage, and Mages might be able to use it as a Yantra, especially for spells relating to addiction, blood or vampires in specific. Sin-Eaters might also be able to use it for a Ceremony. The blood of the dead seems like it'd be a pretty potent symbol for a Bound Ceremony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T10:51:57-07:00","id":1151681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151673#post1151673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably nothing acutally useful would come out of it. It can't ghouls major templates, but I assume they could still get Vitae addicted. Werewolves might be more prone to Death Rage, and willingly drinking vampire blood can't be good for a Changeling's Clarity. Argentum-following Prometheans might actually <i>benefit</i> from experiencing Vitae addiction, in that it could assist in the Pilgrimage, and Mages might be able to use it as a Yantra, especially for spells relating to addiction, blood or vampires in specific. Sin-Eaters might also be able to use it for a Ceremony. The blood of the dead seems like it'd be a pretty potent symbol for a Bound Ceremony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap you just gave me a brilliant idea. A Elder vampire who survived risking topor and Kindred politics from centuries ago by blood-addicting a krewe of Sin-Eaters (and maintaining such a cult through the ages), allowing a on-the-surface mutually-beneficial relationship that enables the Elder to carve out <i>their own Dead Dominion.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:34:58-07:00","id":1151695,"title":"","content":"Vampires can't even instantly heal aggravated damage in themselves like that, they have to rest too.<br /> <br /> But drinking Vitae can addict and blood bond werewolves and other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> That said, it has to be given to them somehow. Vampires don't 'bleed' Vitae, so if you just cut them or bite them you won't get dosed with it unless, like a vampire, your bite attack drains the stuff from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:36:53-07:00","id":1151698,"title":"","content":"There's some useful stuff in the Requiem 1e core, pp. 166-67.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:14:04-07:00","id":1151723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151671#post1151671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically no, but, what do we &quot;mechanically&quot; get out of any drug? That's not why we take them, or want other people addicted to them on our behalf. Speaking for the narrative, the werewolves could think they get a <i>lot</i> out of drinking blood from a vampire, thinking it makes them stronger, faster, or whatever--but it could all be a placebo, built on the powerful lie their addiction is giving them, and the overwhelming feelings it forces them to have for their vampire dealer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in terms of possible werewolf players bait - for example, selling rumor of 'blood drinking let you regenerate even Aggravated wounds' be some really good stuff. Saying 'it's just blood bonds and drug high', would mean that any Uratha elder just say to pups 'Do not use vampire's blood - it's just not worth it and gives nothing to us'. It would not be even 'forbidden fruit' selling point, it's just... poor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-21-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:20:59-07:00","id":1151724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151698#post1151698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some useful stuff in the Requiem 1e core, pp. 166-67.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting 1E corebook text <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar618_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"618\" data-vbnamecard=\"618\">branford</a> mentioned for ease of discussion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR, p. 168</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>THE BLOOD AND OTHER SUPERNATURAL CREATURES</b><br /> Kindred Vitae, while potent, does have its limits. When the other supernatural creatures with whom the Damned occasionally cross paths come into play, certain realities of the World of Darkness supersede the mystic strength of the Blood.<br /> <br /> Werewolves and mages are immune to the Embrace. If a vampire is somehow able to extract all the blood from a werewolf or mage and attempt the Embrace, that Embrace fails automatically. Likewise with Vinculums and attempts at creating ghouls \u2014 they simply do not work with regard to Lupines and mages. Other supernatural creatures are subject to blood addiction, however, the absence of other supernatural effects notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> Naturally, this physiological situation doesn\u2019t deter rumors of such things from spreading. Savvy Kindred who hear of such things, however, wisely dismiss them as the efforts of inexperienced vampires trying to codify something they don\u2019t understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the wolves can have only blood addiction, by RAW. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:30:33-07:00","id":1151732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151724#post1151724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the wolves can have only blood addiction, by RAW. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition, yes. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\">Second edition expanded blood bonds to all supernaturals</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T13:36:16-07:00","id":1151735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151723#post1151723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in terms of possible werewolf players bait - for example, selling rumor of 'blood drinking let you regenerate even Aggravated wounds' be some really good stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're going to want to go for things personalized to your game, because all the benefits Vitae offers non-vampires revolve around establishing a dependency on something you need a vampire to refine.<br /> <br /> Lean into facts like &quot;a lot of Werewolf's ritual symbolism necessitates blood,&quot; &quot;Cr\u00faac blood sorcery is an aesthetically spookier neighbor of the primal magic of the Shadow,&quot; &quot;there's an entire Coil of the Dragon that revolves around the mystical-social benefits of Vitae,&quot; and so on \u2014 the RAW covers the baseline circumstances, but a vampire who's developed or uncovered a way to empower werewolves with their Vitae has a narrative and ecological niche that justifies special effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T14:13:46-07:00","id":1151747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1151723#post1151723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in terms of possible werewolf players bait - for example, selling rumor of 'blood drinking let you regenerate even Aggravated wounds' be some really good stuff. Saying 'it's just blood bonds and drug high', would mean that any Uratha elder just say to pups 'Do not use vampire's blood - it's just not worth it and gives nothing to us'. It would not be even 'forbidden fruit' selling point, it's just... poor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, honestly? I'd think the vast majority of werewolves WOULD tell you to stay away from vampire blood the same way that we were bombarded with DARE campaigns as kids and told to stay away from drugs! What werewolf in their right mind would use vampire blood? We don't take these dangerous drugs for purely rational or good reasons.<br /> <br /> But social pressure and the allure of new experiences is compelling--a unwary werewolf could even simply have their blood spiked by a vampire. Like, imagine someone with cruac doing something where they infected a deer with their blood, and the ritual makes the deer more likely to be hunted--high primal urge werewolf who can only eat meat they freshly killed themselves eats the deer and gets vampire blood into their system, and then reveals how they've addicted the werewolf to themselves in private, and offers a deal--I won't tell your werewolf pack you're tainted if you do some favors for me, and you can have aaaalll the blood you want.<br /> <br /> In short, if you want your players to deal with this, then if you don't homerule something awesome (and I think that's a perfectly reasonable thing to do!), like the regenerating aggravated damage during blood rage as an emergency stim-pack thingy, then you should play it purely for the drama. Like look at how much werewolves already care about &quot;gang issues&quot; like drugs or territory, especially in the Dark Era Bowery Dogs chapter ,and then get thinking of a supernatural variant where the local vampires are getting even packs addicted to their drugs.<br /> <br /> Does your players pack given into the temptation? Or are they fighting against it? What if someone, in secret, agrees to get addicted not for mechanical benefit, but because it creates drama and interesting situations for your troupe and your story? Taking on flaws with no mechanical benefit doesn't make sense as a &quot;game&quot; quality, but, from a story perspective, that's incredibly important! There's a lot to be gained from simply having character flaws---which is why mortals have Vices, afterall (although not perfect because it gives willpower, but, players need sooome kind of carrot for playing suboptimally in the name of the story.)<br /> <br /> Which itself could be the carrot--vampire blood rewarding occassional wp in exchange for making the story more dramatic from a rural fantasy story about werewolves addicted to supernatural drugs?<br /> <br /> I dunno that's just a lot of wild ideas, but, I hope it helps present options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T14:34:05-07:00","id":1151753,"title":"","content":"There's more info concerning the effects of werewolf and mage blood on vampires on the pages cited in Requiem 1e.<br /> <br /> Here's a link to a screenshot of just the two referenced pages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.sendspace.com/file/tqr3we\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sendspace.com/graphics/header/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sendspace.com/file/tqr3we\" target=\"_blank\"> Free large file hosting. Send big files the easy way! </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sendspace.com/file/tqr3we\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.sendspace.com/file/tqr3we </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Free file hosting. Email large files for free. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T20:37:40-07:00","id":1151842,"title":"","content":"I could swear I read somewhere few years back that vampire blood have strange effects on the various monsters - like a sidebar in 1E, or something. Oh, I remember it was the effects on vampire from drinking other monsters blood. It went something like this...<br /> <br /> <b>Monsters blood on vampires effects:</b><ul><li><b>Werewolves</b> - Uratha blood lead Kindred to Rage. Got some penalties to Rages.</li> <li><b>Mages</b> - Awakened blood granted visions to vampires.</li> <li><b>Prometheans </b>- Created blood was no nourishment, as it is not real blood, so vamps got only half of Vitea they could normally take from the plasma they drank.</li> <li><b>Changelings </b>- Lost blood give also strange visions to vampires.</li> </ul>It ended on Changelings, as it was all the gamelines to this date published. I cannot remember where I read this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now if I would make special effects of Kindred blood on monsters in 2E, it would be like this...<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire blood on monsters effects:</b><ul><li><b>Werewolves</b> - They get in to Death Rage. In 2E I would probably start with Wasu-Im and give Aggravated healing for wolves ( 1 Vitea for 1 Aggrav, can exchange 1 point per 1 turn only ), to make things tempting. Burning all Vitea on regeneration would end Wasu-Im - IF Uratha would not go over Basu-Im in meantime.</li> <li><b>Mages</b> - They get some special visions. In 2E I would probably made Vitea as superYantra and/or clearing Opacity of Mysteries, 1 on 1 bonus/penalty basis.</li> <li><b>Prometheans</b> - They got some alchemical process. In 2E maybe they can burn Vitea as once used Vitroil free given to them? Things like sealing Alchemy, etc. - <i>not </i>giving free traits.</li> <li><b>Changelings</b> - Would wait for 2E corebook, but maybe Kindred blood can work as some kind umbrela from True Fae? Or changes Banes of particular Lost character?</li> </ul>In all scenarios I would make <i>Blood Addiction</i> on each monster as Condition the monster character can get Beats in long play, for listening to demands of vampire that feeds him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-22-2017, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:58:37-07:00","id":1152440,"title":"","content":"I can think of several ways to apply such theme on the game with mechanics. I'm going for it quickly, because I have to go to work earlier today.<br /> <br /> First, new material that can be added to work with RAW.<br /> <br /> As there is a Merit for Vampires to take on supernatural blood for a Vampire-like kick, there could be Merits for the opposite effect. A Vampire Merit would make for the Faustian devil, that can empower others with her vitae. Similar effect could be attained with specific Cr\u00faac Rituals or Scales of the Dragon, but a Carthian or Invictus Merit would be an interesting twist for a more political tone. A Theban ritual also could make into the focal point of an All Inclusive cell of the Lancea.<br /> <br /> On the other side, a Merit for the other Supernatural would play either on the themes of predator or addicted. The simplest way is to make a splat able to harness their own energy from Vitae, but I can think of their powers being augmented through this. Lets say, Changeling could devise a way to accomplish a Contract's catch through Vitae.<br /> <br /> Yet another version for the theme of the Victim, a Vampire could have this as a Condition, maybe with the unusual side effect of not binding the other. This monster would become a resource for others, with only her other powers to protect her and grant her leverage.<br /> <br /> Twisting the RAW only a little, the Otherworlds of the setting can make the trick. Vampires are meant only for this earthly realm, but the other splats can take the blood, or the entire victim, to the strange realities where they duel. The Shadow, the Underworld, the Hedge, the Astral Realm. They all have the potential to transmutate whatever is taken there, and the power of the Vitae can make this work in ways stranger still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T12:17:43-07:00","id":1152584,"title":"","content":"One benefit a Werewolf might get (big MIGHT) from tasting Vampire blood would be their ability to track anyone who's blood they have tasted, or instead maybe identify the Vampire's last victim or recognize any of its ghouls or blood bonded mortals by scent.<br /> \u200bIf you just want a way Vampire blood has an effect upon Werewolves in the region then you could house rule that drugs laced with the blood (and alcohol) can affect a Werewolf's hyper metabolism the way they would normal mortals. You were an addict before the change? Now you can still be an addict after.<br /> <br /> For a Changeling option that would make Vitae very tempting, you could house rule that drinking Vampire blood confuses the Huntsman on your tail allowing a quick escape. Perhaps even ending that particular hunt.<br /> I could see an entire freehold addicted to Vitae out of fear of their Keepers.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor a Mage option maybe treat Vitae like a Perfected Material, with traits of its own useful to a Mage. With Death you could also convert it into Mana, unfortunately that Mana will have a resonance of enslavement or addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 10-24-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T03:44:06-07:00","id":1152744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151640-2e-vampire-blood-effects-on-other-supernatural?p=1152584#post1152584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Changeling option that would make Vitae very tempting, you could house rule that drinking Vampire blood confuses the Huntsman on your tail allowing a quick escape. Perhaps even ending that particular hunt.<br /> I could see an entire freehold addicted to Vitae out of fear of their Keepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Others do not sound to me as compelling, but this idea of 'instant free running from Keeper' card is very tempting and cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T14:08:28-07:00","id":1152934,"title":"","content":"Some loose ideas to be worked out. Keep in mind that I didn't read anything from this game for almost a year, so sorry for anything wrong:<br /> <br /> VAMPIRES:<br /> <br /> Merit: Blood of the Tempter:<br /> Supernatural beings that drink of your Vitae get 1 dot in a Discipline of your choice, among the Disciplines that you have. It lasts until next Dawn, and the drinker keeps any Vitae taken for eventual expenditure as a Ghoul, in case it isn't a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Merit: Blood of the Ancient (BP 6+)<br /> For each BP beyond 5, BotT can give 1 more dot in Disciplines, limited to levels you have yourself.<br /> <br /> Merit: Soldarius (Invictus)<br /> You can establish Vassalage with a non-vampire. Your Vassal can turn your Vitae into another thing useful for her, spend it to ask for your power (you can make a single Action with a Discipline as if you stood there), and take normal advantage from other Merits based on Vassalage.<br /> <br /> Merit: Contaminating Idea (Carthian)<br /> If someone drinks your blood, but can't be Ghouled, you can craft for her a Condition named Memetic Blood, with whatever shedding action you want. The Beats gained from this Condition can be used to develop Discipline dots you have. If the person already have a Discipline dot, the Condition can be made Permanent.<br /> <br /> OTHERS:<br /> <br /> Merit: Drink Macabre<br /> You can turn a Vampire's Vitae into Essence/Mana/Glamour/etc.<br /> <br /> Merit: Hyena (Werewolf)<br /> After drinking a Vampire's Vitae, you can access their Predator's Aura effect for a scene, or access the benefits of one of your other forms while in Human or Wolf, also for a scene. You can't do this again until you drink Vitae again, and you loose all benefits at Dawn.<br /> <br /> Merit: Smell of the Hunter (Changelings)<br /> At a night in which you drank a Vampire's Vitae, your very touch is considered Cold Iron for True Fae and Goblins.<br /> (This was really an interesting idea)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T15:03:29-07:00","id":1152954,"title":"","content":"Is the last one a changeling merit or a vampire merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T15:12:14-07:00","id":1154855,"title":"","content":"Changeling's.<br /> <br /> I'll wrap some of those ideas in a Goggle Doc, so I can work them over time. I really like Vampire, and ideas on interactions for the line. With time I'll make a comprehensive document about ways of implementing and using effects both of Vitae on others and of other's blood on Vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GEgKHiWoWH4613gwdIZhAys_Ycb-eEK1fDjNogAGuqs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GEgKHiWoWH4613gwdIZhAys_Ycb-eEK1fDjNogAGuqs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GEgKHiWoWH4613gwdIZhAys_Ycb-eEK1fDjNogAGuqs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GEgKHiWoWH4613gwdIZhAys_Ycb-eEK1fDjNogAGuqs/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}